material: 144 reports (20 of them played live) at Arsenal, Barcelona, Brentford, Bayern Munich
1) Stats equal the committed play: keeper saves off the play list, bookings and changes off their lines
   144 reports and 20 live matches at 20 and 70: 1072 saves (7.44 a match), every one a shot on target that was not a goal, and every booking and change counted off its line
2) The timeline equals the committed play: every chance, save, corner and penalty once, and nothing else
   144 timelines: 1072 saves, 1898 shots off target, 1818 corners and 47 penalties, each one a committed event and none missing
3a) The report card prints the report's own numbers on every stat bar
   1440 stat bars on 144 cards, every one the report's own number both sides
3b) The timeline on the card is the report's own timeline, row for row
   2846 rows on 144 cards, every one the report's own row, the clock rows off the report's own board
4) The live strip prints the saves, bookings and changes so far, never the whole match
   60 live strips (at 20, at 70, at the whistle), 28 of them with bookings or changes still to come, every one the engine's count at its minute
5) Nothing the sim does not model is on either screen
   16 stat labels on the two screens (Possession, Shots, On target, Expected goals, Corners, Fouls, Keeper saves, Yellow cards, Red cards, Substitutions, Shots (on target), xG, Saves, Yellow, Red, Subs), none of them a number the sim does not draw
simCmMatchCentre: PASS. Every stat on the report and the live strip is counted off the committed play and lines, and every timeline row is an event the engine drew.
